  "caption": "3am: Quinn woke to a hot, swollen big toe. No injury, so Quinn guessed a sprain.\n\nIt may be gout, where crystals inflame a joint — often the big toe. It builds over hours, often settles over one to two weeks, and needs a medical diagnosis.\n\nWhat can help: see your GP for a first attack with no injury, don't massage or stretch the hot joint (rest, elevate and offload it), go easy on beer, spirits and sugary drinks, avoid crash diets, get a GP review even once it settles, and rebuild walking in roomy, cushioned shoes.\n\nGet same-day help if a hot, swollen joint comes with fever, chills, spreading redness or feeling unwell.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
